  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given NNN non-negative integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​. You are allowed to perform following operation any number of times:\n\n\nChoose any valid index iii (1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N) and a positive integer M&gt;0M&gt;0M&gt;0 and replace AiA_iAi​ with Ai mod MA_i\\bmod MAi​modM. That is, replace AiA_iAi​ with its remainder when divided by MMM, which is a value between 000 and M−1M-1M−1, inclusive.\nMMM does not need to be same between different operations.\nFind the minimum number of operations to make all the array elements **equal**.\n\n**Note:** Since the input and output are large, prefer using fast input-output methods.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains an integer TTT - the number of test cases. Then TTT test cases follow.\nThe first line of each test case contains an integer NNN - the size of array.\nThe second line contains NNN integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ - the elements of the array.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test, print one line containing an integer which denotes minimum number of operations performed to make all the elements equal.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "0≤Ai≤2⋅1090 \\leq A_i \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^90≤Ai​≤2⋅109",
      "It is guaranteed that the sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 10610^6106."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n3\n2 1 3\n3\n1 1 3",
        "output": "3\n1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nIn first test case, we can make all the elements equal by following operations:\n\nTake i=1i = 1i=1 and M=2M = 2M=2 and do A1:=A1 mod 2=0A_1 := A_1 \\bmod 2 = 0A1​:=A1​mod2=0.\nTake i=2i = 2i=2 and M=1M = 1M=1 and do A2:=A2 mod 1=0A_2 := A_2 \\bmod 1 = 0A2​:=A2​mod1=0.\nTake i=3i = 3i=3 and M=3M = 3M=3 and do A3:=A3 mod 3=0A_3 := A_3 \\bmod 3 = 0A3​:=A3​mod3=0.\nAfter these 333 operations we have all the elements equal to zero.\n\nIn second test case, we can perform following operation:\n\nChoose i=3i = 3i=3 and M=2M = 2M=2 and do A3:=A3 mod 2=1A_3 := A_3 \\bmod 2 = 1A3​:=A3​mod2=1.\nAfter this operation all the elements are 111."
      }
    ]
  },
